      "question": "Find the slope of the line passing through (-2, 3) and (4, 9).",
      "choices": {
        "A": "1",
        "B": "2",
        "C": "3",
        "D": "-1",
        "E": "1/2"
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "explanation": "Slope = (y₂ - y₁)/(x₂ - x₁) = (9 - 3)/(4 - (-2)) = 6/6 = 1.",
      "steps": [
        "1. Use slope formula: m = (y₂ - y₁)/(x₂ - x₁).",
        "2. Substitute: (9 - 3)/(4 - (-2)).",
        "3. Calculate: 6/6 = 1."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Slope: rise over run between two points."
    },
